// src/pages/outdoor/brands/coyote.astro
// Coyote grill brand page. Built to twin-eagles.astro / bull.astro pattern.
// Verified model codes only (site scrape): C1CHCS, C3C30, C3C34, C3CH36, C3CL36, C3CL42, C3CO50,
//   C3SL30, C3SL36, C3SL42. Two main gas lines: C-Series (value built-in, C3C...) and S-Series (C3SL...,
//   RapidSear infrared burner + illuminated/LED control knobs + interior grill lights). Coyote Outdoor Living (US).
// Do NOT over-interpret every suffix; describe the two lines and the features that are real (RapidSear, LED knobs, interior lights).
// Em-dash budget in visible body: keep low. Voice: "our techs" / "we". $89 outdoor diagnostic.

import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ServiceHero from '../../../components/ServiceHero.astro';
import { MAIN_PHONE } from '../../../data/branches';

import { mergeCredentials } from '../../../data/credentials-schema';
import { BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL } from '../../../lib/build-location-array';
const phone = MAIN_PHONE;
const phoneRaw = MAIN_PHONE.replace(/\D/g, '');
const phoneHref = `tel:+1${phoneRaw}`;
const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/outdoor/brands/coyote/";

const title = "Coyote Grill Repair Los Angeles — Same Day";
const description = `Coyote grill repair across Southern California. C-Series and S-Series built-ins, RapidSear infrared, LED-lit knobs. C3SL, C3C, C3CL. $89 diagnostic. ${phone}.`;

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What Coyote grills do you repair in Los Angeles?",
    a: "The Coyote built-in gas grill lineup: the C-Series (value built-in, model codes like C3C30, C3C34, and the C3CL and C3CO built-in variants) and the S-Series (the C3SL30, C3SL36, and C3SL42, with the RapidSear infrared burner, illuminated control knobs, and interior grill lights). Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair service both lines across all seven Southern California counties, natural gas and liquid propane."
  },
  {
    q: "What is the RapidSear burner on my Coyote S-Series, and why does it fail differently?",
    a: "The S-Series (C3SL models) includes a RapidSear infrared burner that the value C-Series does not have. Infrared burners run far hotter and cycle harder than the standard tube burners around them, so they wear out earlier, usually the ceramic element or the ignition feeding it. When a Coyote sear zone quits while the main burners work, our techs diagnose the RapidSear burner, its orifice, and its ignition separately. It is a different part and a different repair than a standard burner."
  },
  {
    q: "The LED-lit knobs or interior lights on my Coyote stopped working. Can you fix that?",
    a: "Usually yes, and these are on a separate circuit from the gas system. The S-Series illuminated control knobs and the interior grill lights fail at the LED and wiring stage, not at the burners. Our techs diagnose the light circuit separately, so a lighting fault does not get misread as a bigger problem. These are inexpensive parts. If the grill also has an ignition or burner issue, we handle that on the same visit."
  },
  {
    q: "One zone on my Coyote won't light. New grill needed?",
    a: "Almost never. A single dead zone with the others working is usually the ignition electrode for that burner, or a burner orifice fouled after seasons without a cover. Our techs test the electrode, the ignition, and the gas flow in sequence rather than guessing, and replace the one part that failed. Coyote parts are widely available and inexpensive, so most of these finish same-day. $89 outdoor diagnostic, waived with repair."
  },
  {
    q: "How long do Coyote grills last, and are parts easy to get?",
    a: "With repair and maintenance, a Coyote built-in gives 12 to 18 years, longer inland than on the coast. Coyote is a mid-premium brand with widely available parts, so burners, electrodes, the RapidSear infrared burner, and the LED components are inexpensive and we often source them quickly. Salt air on coastal installs in Malibu and Newport Beach is the main limiter, and we replace corroding burners early before the manifold takes damage."
  },
  {
    q: "My Coyote is built into an island. Does that change the repair?",
    a: "Access changes, the diagnosis does not. Our techs work the built-in C-Series and S-Series grills from the front of a BBQ island, swapping burners, electrodes, and the RapidSear infrared burner without pulling the whole grill out of the surround. On LP setups we confirm the regulator and gas line before re-firing each zone. $89 outdoor diagnostic, waived with repair."
  },
  {
    q: "What's your warranty on Coyote repairs?",
    a: "Ninety days SDAR parts-and-labor warranty on the work we perform. Coyote carries manufacturer coverage on many grill components, so if the failure looks warranty-eligible we tell you before any out-of-pocket work and help you process the claim. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified, and BBB Accredited Business."
  }
];

